   "agent": "auto",
   "prompt": "Owner: autopilot ON by default for every active project; a project with ready tickets and free slots is never idle. Today autopilot (tools/autopilot.mjs, runAutopilot, autopilot-lock.mjs, autopilot-ready-deps.mjs, `swarm autopilot` in tools/swarm.mjs) only runs when someone starts it. Make the board server (tools/board-server or the module that hosts `swarm board`/watch; find it with grep) supervise one autopilot loop per ACTIVE registered project (listProjects in tools/projects.mjs; skip scratch roots via isScratchRoot, skip projects with an unapproved ledger or no tickets, skip a project whose .swarm/autopilot/off file exists). Use the existing acquireAutopilotLock so a manually started autopilot or a second board never double-runs; a loop that loses the lock backs off. Autopilot's action set and its limits stay exactly as they are (it never merges, deploys, raises a cap, approves a scope, or calls a model beyond what a started wave does; spend caps unchanged). Add `swarm autopilot off|on|status [--root]` to toggle the off file and show per-project state, and make `swarm status` print one line 'autopilot: on|off|running' . Also add the idle rule to the board data: a project that has ready tickets and free lane slots but no running run gets an `idleWithReady: true` flag and a line in swarm status (read-only; the board owner will render it). Tests: supervisor starts a loop per active project and not for scratch/unapproved/no-ticket/off projects, lock contention backs off, off/on commands, idle flag. Inject clocks and fakes; no real timers or processes (deterministic, no flakes). Keep tests/autopilot-*.test.mjs passing.",
